                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "createdOn": 1779409215,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Redfish has https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/EnvironmentMetrics.v1_6_0.json \n\nFrom https://redfish.dmtf.org/redfish/mockups/v1/1819\n```\n\"PowerWatts\":view details {\n  \"Reading\":view details 374,\n  \"DataSourceUri\":view details \"/redfish/v1/Chassis/1U/Sensors/TotalPower\"} ,\n\"PowerLimitWatts\":view details {\n  \"SetPoint\":view details 500,\n  \"AllowableMax\":view details 1000,\n  \"AllowableMin\":view details 150,\n  \"ControlMode\":view details \"Automatic\",\n  \"DataSourceUri\":view details \"/redfish/v1/Chassis/1U/Controls/PowerLimit\"} ,\n```\n\nIs there any advice from Redfish on when to use MinPowerWatts / MaxPowerWatts here and when to use EnvironmentMetrics ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 64,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks a lot for catching this and for the EnvironmentMetrics pointer - that was a real semantic mismatch on my side.\nControl.Power.Cap (SetPoint / AllowableMin / AllowableMax) clearly belongs on EnvironmentMetrics.PowerLimitWatts as the mockup shows. To wire Chassis.MinPowerWatts / MaxPowerWatts up correctly, I have added MinPowerWatts / MaxPowerWatts to Inventory.Item.Accelerator (PDI 90569) for the device-spec power range, and this patch now reads from that interface instead. Thanks again for the careful review!\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/90569\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/90462"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 664,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "ChassisUUID is already called here..?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 664,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, thanks for review."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 760,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Can this be a separate function ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 760,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, thanks for review."
                }
            ],
